  "analysis": "Fixed 5 m square patches anchored at the upper left of each released stabilized ROI. A cell at a cropped boundary is counted even if partially visible. Occupancy uses only each enrolled pedestrian\u2019s current unfiltered point. To audit causal context, count same-cell author-tracked points of other pedestrians at strictly earlier frame times, and within the preceding 23 source frames (<=1 s); target ID always excluded. No future coordinate, forecast, score or fitted model is used. The original 3066 IDs were selected using future track completeness, and this remains a selection limitation.",
  "interpretation": "One shared-space site with eleven separately stabilized camera references, per-clip pixel/metric ratios and ROI origins. No common georeferencing transform between those clips established; sum of nonempty cells counts clip-local cells, not unique geographical patches. Point occupancy is an empirical use trace, not a walkway, curb, lane marking or permanent traversability polygon. Full-video supplied GSOC background could incorporate future frames; a prospective map must use image frames available at or before the current prediction and omit the target\u2019s own future.",
